 "operation": [
  {
   "topic": "Families",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "The 16 A triacs come in five families. BTB16 is in TO-220AB with the tab tied to A2; BTA16 is the same in the insulated TO-220AB; T1610, T1635 and T1650 are D²PAK surface-mount parts. Each comes rated 600 V or 800 V repetitive off-state (VDRM/VRRM)."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Standard and Snubberless types",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "The B and C suffixes are standard triacs that trigger in all four quadrants, with IGT up to 50 mA and 25 mA. The W suffixes and the T16 parts are Snubberless: they trigger in quadrants I, II and III only and have very high commutation capability, which suits them to inductive loads. SW and T1610 are the logic-level 10 mA type; CW and T1635 are 35 mA; BW and T1650 are 50 mA."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Uses",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Named applications: static relays, heating regulation, induction motor starting, light dimmers and appliance motor speed controllers, as on/off or phase-angle control on AC mains."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Insulated tab",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "In the BTA16 an internal ceramic pad separates the die from the tab, which is rated to 2500 VRMS of isolation. The BTA series is certified to UL1557, file E81734. Its junction-to-case resistance is 2.1 °C/W against 1.2 °C/W for the other packages, and its 16 A RMS rating holds to a case temperature of 86 °C rather than 100 °C."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Construction",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "The die is clip bonded, which keeps thermal resistance low. Packages are RoHS (2002/95/EC) compliant."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Gate drive",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "Gate current is rated by its maximum IGT at VD = 12 V; the lowest IGT any part has is 5 % of that maximum. A gate held below VGD = 0.2 V does not trigger at 125 °C with full VDRM applied. Peak gate current is 4 A for 20 µs and average gate power 1 W. For the 50 A/µs dI/dt rating the gate is driven at twice IGT with a rise time of 100 ns or less. IGT, IH and IL fall as the junction warms: IGT roughly doubles at -40 °C and drops to under half at 125 °C."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Commutation",
   "page": 3,
   "text": "Standard types are rated for (dV/dt)c at (dI/dt)c = 7 A/ms. Snubberless CW, BW and T1635/T1650 types are rated without any snubber at 8.5 A/ms and 14 A/ms; the SW and T1610 types are rated at a set (dV/dt)c of 0.1 V/µs or 10 V/µs. Allowed (dI/dt)c rises as (dV/dt)c is made slower and as the junction runs cooler, about six times higher near 10 °C than at 125 °C."
  },
  {
   "topic": "On-state loss",
   "page": 5,
   "text": "The maximum on-state curve at Tj max is the straight-line model VTO = 0.85 V plus RD = 25 mΩ. Maximum dissipation at 16 A RMS is about 18.6 W."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Surge",
   "page": 5,
   "text": "A single full 50 Hz cycle may reach 160 A peak from Tj = 25 °C, falling toward 28 A after 1000 cycles; repeated surges at Tc = 85 °C are held to the lower curve. For half-sine pulses shorter than 10 ms the allowed peak rises until the 50 A/µs rise-rate limit sets the ceiling. The fusing I²t is 144 A²s at 10 ms."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Mounting",
   "page": 8,
   "text": "TO-220AB, insulated or not: the epoxy meets UL 94 V0 and cooling is by conduction. Mounting screw torque is 0.55 N·m recommended and 0.70 N·m maximum. Resin gate protrusion on either package is at most 0.5 mm, at one of two marked spots or their mirror images."
  },
  {
   "topic": "D²PAK copper",
   "page": 6,
   "text": "The D²PAK is cooled through copper under its tab on an FR4 board with 35 µm copper. Rth(j-a) is 45 °C/W with 2 cm² and falls to about 28 °C/W at 40 cm². With 1 cm² the part carries about 3 A RMS at 0 °C ambient, derating to zero at 125 °C."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Part number",
   "page": 13,
   "text": "BTA16 and BTB16: BT, then A (insulated) or B (non-insulated), 16 for 16 A, the voltage 600 or 800, the sensitivity and type code (B 50 mA, C 25 mA standard; BW 50 mA, CW 35 mA Snubberless; SW 10 mA logic level), then RG for tube. D²PAK parts: T16, the sensitivity 10, 35 or 50 (mA), the voltage 600 or 800, G for D²PAK, then -TR for tape and reel or nothing for tube."
  }
 ],
